  "notes": "Band-written, conversational, pop-craft country — \"BPM 56–102 straight on 2&4 — the slowest-clustered band in the section,\" so this model's ceiling sits below the genre's own mode. The drums carry a stated negative as their identity: \"a very low fill count. Model minimal variation — these records are groove-static by design,\" over \"a live kit with a programmed clap or snap doubling the snare, 16th shaker, cross-stick verses.\" That is the longest fill spacing here with `fillBeforeSection` off and a hat fill near the floor. Harmony is intentionally flat and the entry says why: \"I–V–vi–IV and I–IV–I–V as short loops, with ii–V turnarounds; the harmony is intentionally plain so the lyric lands.\" The bass is the one busy part: \"syncopated and melodic (pop-rock rather than country root-fifth), mixed forward,\" so root-following drops well below the boom-chick default. Melody is \"mid-tenor, talk-sung verses at conversational density opening to a repeated short chorus cell; group harmony on the hook,\" and the entry adds that \"the guitar riff is the record's identity as often as the vocal hook,\" which is the counter's answer-and-arp weighting. ⚠ The light synth sub on the later singles is reinforcement under a live bass, so no `drums.bass808` block is authored. ⚠ Confidence is medium, matching the research; the per-track readings are [LOW-CONF]. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the snap offsets, the perc density and the counter ratio.",
